# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CONJURE_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Keyless open-weight models (no API key): any OpenAI-compatible server you run —
# Ollama (default), llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, or an internal gateway.
# Used for the forge loop when no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, instead of the offline mock.
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# CONJURE_PROVIDER=open-weights        # force open weights even when a Claude key exists
# With neither of the two set, the forge loop shares the conjure-llm gateway that predictions
# use (CONJURE_LLM_URL, _KEY, _MODEL, _ACCESS_ID, _ACCESS_SECRET, _REASONING): free open-weight
# models with no extra settings.
#
# Resilience (see src/resilience.js, identical copy in scalvs-ai api/_resilience.js):
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_URL may list several servers, comma-separated — requests
# fail over between them. Retryable statuses retry with backoff (Retry-After is
# honoured); a dead server trips a circuit breaker and is skipped while it cools down.
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_RETRIES=2
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_RETRY_BASE_MS=400
# CONJURE_OPEN_WEIGHTS_REDACT=off      # default: credentials in prompts are stripped before they are sent

# Conjure Search (POST /v1/search, and "Research the web first" on forecasts): Yandex Search API, in Russia.
# On the Yandex VM it signs in with the VM's service account (needs the search-api.webSearch.user role) and
# uses CONJURE_LLM_PROJECT as the folder. Elsewhere set a key and folder. CONJURE_SEARCH=off turns it off.
# CONJURE_SEARCH_KEY=
# CONJURE_SEARCH_FOLDER=
# CONJURE_SEARCH_DAILY_LIMIT=1000
# VEIL Search, Infinitum's own engine (no key needed). Used when Yandex isn't set up, and takes over if Yandex fails.
# VEIL_SEARCH_URL=https://infinitumveil.app/api/search
